    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I don't think it's a slump, though. It's more... final. Like, why stay for the decay? Why wait for the hands to shake and the mind to dim until you're just a shadow of the person who made this? There's a certain dignity in stopping when you're still whole, isn't there? To leave while the light is still bright, instead of waiting for the darkness to take it away.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
